# Creating a note reads the whole workspace again, which tells the agenda to query again
# (items/reset). The agenda hears that at once, not with the next change: when the two came
# together, it queried, found the new task already there, and then added it a second time.
size 140x30
env COLD_LAVA_EDITOR=none
env COLD_LAVA_TODAY=2026-11-07
wait-for example-workspace
keys A
wait-for ↑↓ move · x tick · ⏎ open
expect-not ▾ Today
keys g j enter
wait-for Ctrl-o ⟵ agenda
keys n
wait-for new note · Tab template · ⏎ create · Esc cancel
type Ash fall
keys enter
wait-for created Journal/Ash fall.md
write Inbox/Chores.md - [ ] Sweep the ash off the roof 📅 2026-11-07\n
keys ctrl+o
wait-for Ctrl-o ⟵ agenda
keys ctrl+o
wait-for ▾ Today · Sat 7 Nov  1
expect ☐ Sweep the ash off the roof
screen
keys q q
exits 0
